            {
              "id": "glog-baabb51d-8cb8-4d35-b11c-cbb75321cbc0",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe \"Detected Issue with C Function (malloc)\" vulnerability in C++ arises when the `malloc` function is used improperly, leading to potential memory allocation issues. Specifically, using `malloc(sizeof(cl_device_id))` can be problematic if `cl_device_id` is not a primitive type or if its size is not correctly calculated. This can result in buffer overflows, memory corruption, or undefined behavior if the allocated memory is insufficient for the intended use.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Use `sizeof` Correctly**: Ensure that `sizeof` is used with the correct type or object to allocate the appropriate amount of memory.\n2. **Check Return Values**: Always check the return value of `malloc` to ensure that memory allocation was successful.\n3. **Use Safer Alternatives**: Consider using C++ memory management features like `new` or smart pointers (`std::unique_ptr`, `std::shared_ptr`) for automatic memory management.\n4. **Initialize Allocated Memory**: Use functions like `calloc` or `memset` to initialize memory if necessary.\n5. **Free Allocated Memory**: Ensure that all allocated memory is properly freed to avoid memory leaks.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIf `cl_device_id` is a type that requires more than a simple `sizeof` calculation, ensure that the correct size is used. If `cl_device_id` is a complex type, consider using an array or a container that can handle its size dynamically.\n\n```cpp\n#include <CL/cl.h> // OpenCL library\n\n// Corrected memory allocation\ncl_device_id* device_ids = (cl_device_id*)malloc(sizeof(cl_device_id) * number_of_devices);\nif (device_ids == NULL) {\n    // Handle allocation failure\n}\n\n// Use the allocated memory\n\n// Free the allocated memory\nfree(device_ids);\n```\n\n### Library Dependencies\n\nTo execute the code example properly, the following library is required:\n\n- OpenCL library (`CL/cl.h`)\n\n### Relevant Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-122: Heap-based Buffer Overflow](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/122.html)\n- [CWE-131: Incorrect Calculation of Buffer Size](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/131.html)"
              },
