            {
              "id": "glog-5430fee7-d4b9-4d71-a817-d5d4b5588ee4",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe \"Detected Issue with C Function (malloc)\" vulnerability in C++ arises when the `malloc` function is used incorrectly, potentially leading to memory allocation issues such as buffer overflows, memory leaks, or undefined behavior. In the provided code snippet, the `malloc` function is used to allocate memory for a `cl_platform_id` object. If the size of `cl_platform_id` is not properly calculated or if the allocation is not checked for success, it can lead to vulnerabilities.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Check for Allocation Success**: Always check if the memory allocation was successful by verifying that the returned pointer is not `NULL`.\n2. **Use `sizeof` Correctly**: Ensure that the `sizeof` operator is used correctly to allocate the right amount of memory.\n3. **Free Allocated Memory**: Always free the allocated memory when it is no longer needed to prevent memory leaks.\n4. **Consider Safer Alternatives**: Use safer alternatives like `new` in C++ or smart pointers which automatically manage memory.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n```cpp\n#include <CL/cl.h> // OpenCL library for cl_platform_id\n\nint main() {\n    // Correctly allocate memory for cl_platform_id\n    cl_platform_id* platform = (cl_platform_id*)malloc(sizeof(cl_platform_id));\n    \n    // Check if allocation was successful\n    if (platform == NULL) {\n        // Handle allocation failure\n        return -1;\n    }\n\n    // Use the platform...\n\n    // Free the allocated memory\n    free(platform);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n### Library Dependencies\n\n- OpenCL library (`CL/cl.h`): Required for the `cl_platform_id` type.\n\n### Relevant Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration\n\n- [CWE-401: Improper Release of Memory Before Removing Last Reference ('Memory Leak')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/401.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)"
