            {
              "id": "glog-d829b6e2-6af4-4f65-8339-9c0b1033adf5",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description of \"Unsecured URL\" Vulnerability in C++ Programming Language\n\nAn \"Unsecured URL\" vulnerability occurs when a program uses URLs that are not protected by secure protocols, such as HTTPS. This can lead to various security issues, including man-in-the-middle attacks, where an attacker intercepts and potentially alters the communication between the client and server. In C++ applications, this vulnerability can arise when using libraries or functions that handle URL requests without enforcing secure protocols.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Use HTTPS**: Always use HTTPS instead of HTTP to ensure that data is encrypted during transmission.\n2. **Validate URLs**: Ensure that URLs are validated and sanitized before use.\n3. **Use Secure Libraries**: Utilize libraries that support secure connections and have built-in mechanisms for handling secure URLs.\n4. **Certificate Validation**: Implement proper certificate validation to prevent man-in-the-middle attacks.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nBelow is an example of how to fix an unsecured URL vulnerability in C++ by using a secure library that supports HTTPS:\n\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n#include <curl/curl.h>\n\n// Function to perform a secure HTTPS request\nvoid performSecureRequest(const std::string& url) {\n    CURL* curl;\n    CURLcode res;\n\n    curl_global_init(CURL_GLOBAL_DEFAULT);\n    curl = curl_easy_init();\n\n    if(curl) {\n        curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_URL, url.c_str());\n        \n        // Enforce HTTPS\n        curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_USE_SSL, CURLUSESSL_ALL);\n        \n        // Perform the request\n        res = curl_easy_perform(curl);\n\n        // Check for errors\n        if(res != CURLE_OK) {\n            std::cerr << \"curl_easy_perform() failed: \" << curl_easy_strerror(res) << std::endl;\n        }\n\n        // Clean up\n        curl_easy_cleanup(curl);\n    }\n\n    curl_global_cleanup();\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::string secureUrl = \"https://www.cygnus-software.com\";\n    performSecureRequest(secureUrl);\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n### Library Dependencies\n\nTo execute the above code example, the following library dependencies are required:\n\n- `libcurl`: A free and easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library, supporting HTTPS.\n\n### OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Transport Layer Protection Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transport_Layer_Protection_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices - Quick Reference Guide](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
